Title:
Helium SAE (Tong-Lin) 800nm 6fs Gaussian intensity scan point 01 of 10  I=1.544e+14 Wcm2 z-pol

# He 1s ionised by an ANALYTIC GAUSSIAN 800 nm, 6 fs FWHM pulse, velocity gauge, z-pol.
# Physics: E0=0.0663 au, Up=0.339 au=9.2 eV, quiver alpha=20.5 au,
#   Keldysh gamma=1.154, barrier u=E0/E_b=0.32 (E_b=Ip^2/4=0.2041 au).
# BOX=80 = max(80, ~1.5*alpha) so the box exceeds the quiver (else the electron sloshes across
#   the absorber and the yield is badly under-estimated). ECS theta=0.15 for strong-field stability.
# fixStep=0.0272 = 2.0/Emax, Emax=(sqrt(2*cutEnergy)+aPeak)^2/2=73 au (RK |E|dt<2.83).

#define BOX 80.

# Tong-Lin SAE He: Zc=1, a1=1.231,a2=0.662,a3=-1.325,a4=1.236,a5=-0.231,a6=0.480 (a3,a5<0 -> minus)
#define TongLinHeV (1.0+1.231*exp(-0.662*Q)-1.325*Q*exp(-1.236*Q)-0.231*exp(-0.480*Q))/Q

# No Spectrum/iSurff: total yield + time trace only -> single propagation pass, complete expec trace.
# Radial split [0,2],[2,20],[20,BOX] keeps r=20 (the chi[0,20] sphere) on an element boundary.
Axis: name,order,lowerEnd,upperEnd,functions,nElem
 Phi,1
 Eta,30,-1,1,assocLegendre{Phi}
 Rn,14,0.,2.,polynomial,3
 Rn,12,2.,20.,RpowL*polynomial,4
 Rn,12,20.,BOX,RpowL*polynomial,14
 Rn,30,BOX,Infty,polExp[0.5]

Absorption: kind, axis, theta, radius
ECS,Rn,0.15,BOX

Operator: hamiltonian=1/2<<Laplacian>>+<1><1><-TongLinHeV>
Operator: interaction='iLaserAz[t]<<D/DZ>>'
Operator: expectationValue='<1><1><chi[0,20]>'

# He 1s ground state (l=0). Confirm "Initial <H0>: -0.9038" before trusting.
Initial: state=0

# analytic Gaussian envelope, FWHM(intensity) = 6.0 fs = 2.24844 OptCyc, propagated +-3 FWHM.
Laser: shape, I(W/cm2), FWHM, lambda(nm)
gauss, 1.5445e+14, 2.24844 OptCyc, 800.

# begin/end explicit: a Gaussian has infinite support (auto range would be infinite). +-3 FWHM captures
# it to ~4e-6 of peak. store>=fixStep so the expec trace writes fully.
TimePropagation: begin,end,print,store,cutEnergy,operatorThreshold,fixStep
 -6.74533 OptCyc,6.74533 OptCyc,0.25 OptCyc,0.05,60,1e-9,0.0272
